From: ProjectM TV maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve original circle spacing and pre-smoothing closure

MilkDrop2 unblended circle uses i/(240-1)*6.28 for 240 angular
samples, then duplicates the first vertex before shared smoothing:
241 raw points become 481 smoothed points and draw as a strip.
Preserve PCM/window smoothing, first-tenth seam-radius blending,
6.28f/time/aspect/mystery inputs, Native line/dot style and density
policies, evaluated modes and one-producer prepared geometry replay.

The TV pipeline fades separately rendered presets; this does not emulate
original geometry-blended waves, where MilkDrop suppresses the duplicate.
No shared smoothing change, equation evaluation, new pass or target.

Original: vis_milk2/milkdropfs.cpp:2899-2923,3319-3334,3359-3365.

--- a/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/Waveforms/Circle.cpp
+++ b/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/Waveforms/Circle.cpp
@@ -10,7 +10,8 @@
 
 auto Circle::IsLoop() -> bool
 {
-    return true;
+    // Closure is an explicit endpoint before smoothing, drawn as a strip.
+    return false;
 }
 
 auto Circle::UsesNormalizedMysteryParam() -> bool
@@ -23,11 +24,11 @@
 {
     m_samples = Audio::WaveformSamples / 2;
 
-    m_wave1Vertices.resize(m_samples);
+    m_wave1Vertices.resize(m_samples + 1);
 
     const int sampleOffset{(Audio::WaveformSamples - m_samples) / 2};
 
-    const float inverseSamplesMinusOne{1.0f / static_cast<float>(m_samples)};
+    const float inverseSamplesMinusOne{1.0f / static_cast<float>(m_samples - 1)};
 
     for (int i = 0; i < m_samples; i++)
     {
@@ -45,6 +46,10 @@
             radius * cosf(angle) * m_aspectY + m_waveX,
             radius * sinf(angle) * m_aspectX + m_waveY};
     }
+
+    // MilkDrop closes the unblended circle before its common smoothing pass.
+    m_wave1Vertices[m_samples] = m_wave1Vertices.front();
+    ++m_samples;
 }
 
 } // namespace Waveforms

